0..78 Comment "// An eliminator that writes its answer, `if c -> C { … }` or `case e -> C {"
79..158 Comment "// … }`, answers it wherever it stands: the case is ascribed the answer, so a"
159..235 Comment "// computation a `run` binds and a source\'s run target, which state no type,"
236..313 Comment "// synthesise it, and each arm is checked against it (#2089). The rule is the"
314..384 Comment "// annotation rule of bidirectional typing (Dunfield and Krishnaswami,"
385..455 Comment "// \"Bidirectional Typing\", ACM Computing Surveys 54(5), 2021, § 3: an"
456..502 Comment "// annotated term synthesises its annotation)."
504..578 Comment "/// A conditional a `run` binds: its written answer types the bound value."
